Add an opt-in scene curve before spectral film upsampling.

Selective adaptation of main d4b8145f6f9bdade15cda014776e99521adf0b5f:
https://github.com/JamesQiu2005/SpektraLab/blob/d4b8145f6f9bdade15cda014776e99521adf0b5f/engine/src/pipeline/scene_latitude.cpp
https://github.com/JamesQiu2005/SpektraLab/blob/d4b8145f6f9bdade15cda014776e99521adf0b5f/engine/src/shaders/scene_latitude.metal

Keep the legacy exposure_baseline_ev and Scene Latitude APIs. Empty curve
text skips the new node completely. Non-empty tables are SHOOT edits with
five rows (rgb/luma/r/g/b), evaluated on +/-8 film-exposure stops. Preserve
the original auto-meter -> placement -> curve -> upsample -> exposure order.
Port the same gain algorithm to Vulkan with precise arithmetic and Android's
push-constant base for chunked 1D dispatch. Limit mobile input to 4096 samples per row and 1 MiB text, and
reject incomplete CSV, nonfinite values and embedded NUL.
The companion 0030 patch clears the scene curve in medium_probe_params so
the independent film/paper reference probe does not inherit an image edit.
Co-created with GPT (OpenAI), 2026-11-09.

